WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.834
-Our next guest can be seen

00:00:01.834 --> 00:00:03.467
on his nationwide stand-up tour,

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.667
that includes a night

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:07.367
at the Vivint Arena
in Salt Lake City --

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:09.234
an Arena, oh, my goodness,
how fun --

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:10.434
November 24th.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.901
Please welcome the very funny
Ryan Hamilton!

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:16.534
[ The Roots playing funk ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:22.634
♪♪

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:25.234
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.300
Hi. You're not
going to believe this.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.634
I'm from Idaho.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:31.033
[ Cheering and applause ]
Maybe you do believe that.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:33.934
It's strange.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:36.400
That's enough to get a laugh
in New York City, really.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.634
[ Laughter ]
It doesn't really register
here, you know?

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.968
It's just people go, right now,
are looking at me, going,

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:44.300
"This guy from Iowa
is pretty interesting."

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.467
[ Laughter ]
That's how it is.
I love this city,

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:49.133
but it's not my default setting,
you know?

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.501
There's a rhythm to this city

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:54.701
that I have to get into
and I can feel it coming.

00:00:54.701 --> 00:00:57.901
My chest starts to tighten up,
my thoughts start to whirl.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.868
It's like I'm getting
into double Dutch.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:02.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
I can feel it.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:04.534
It's like,
"I'm going to New York.

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:06.133
[ Laughter ]
I'm going to New York.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.334
I'm in New York.
I'm in New York.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.834
[ Laughter and applause ]
Don't touch me.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:11.167
[ Cheering ]

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:15.334
I don't have any money.
I don't have any money.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:16.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:18.334
Hold the door, please.
Hold the door.

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:19.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.834
This is a two-bedroom?
Are you out of your mind?"

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:24.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:27.667
But make no mistake --
this is an improvisational city.

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:30.400
I mean, you leave your house
and you're scatting, you know?

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.901
[ Laughter ]
Subway's down, Uber's surging.

00:01:32.901 --> 00:01:33.801
I'm running.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.334
This is the only city you go,
"I guess I'm going to run."

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:38.467
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.234
It's just another mode
of transportation.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.667
[ Laughter ]
People just run here, you know?

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:43.534
And people get it.

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.033
"What happened?"
I ran 40 blocks.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:47.334
People go, "Oh, I'm so sorry.
I had to run yesterday.

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:48.400
Isn't it terrible?"

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:54.834
I saw a guy running on the
George Washington Bridge

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.667
and not an exercise guy...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.400
...a suit guy, just running.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:05.000
If you see an exercise guy
on a bridge,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.534
you think,
"That guy is ambitious."

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.901
But if you see
a suit guy running --

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:12.501
just about anywhere,
but especially on a bridge --

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.734
you think,
"That guy's in trouble."

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:20.868
Where are you in your life that
you're in a suit and you go,

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.467
"I'm on the wrong side
of the river!

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:23.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:25.133
Oh, no!

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.434
Oh, no!

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.901
Not again!"

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:30.868
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:35.467
I think that guy's dead.
I don't know.

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:42.167
I saw a guy on the subway
holding a Citi Bike

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.534
and I can't stop thinking
about that guy.

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:46.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:47.834
I was just looking at him like,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.067
"I don't know
where you're going,

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.934
but I know there's a better way
to get there.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:51.834
I know."

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:58.033
I mean, if you don't know,
Citi Bikes are these free bikes

00:02:58.033 --> 00:02:59.767
we have around the city
that you pay for.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:03.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.834
You know them.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.801
He was on public transportation

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:10.234
and holding
public transportation.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:11.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:14.467
It was so perplexing, you know?

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.634
What are you doing?
Did you pay twice?

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.434
[ Laughter ]
I don't understand.

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.200
It's very strange because we all

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.868
make our travel plan
in the morning, you know?

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.167
Like I'm going to take
this down and transfer there.

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.501
And this guy had to be like...

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:30.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.601
..."I'm overwhelmed.
I don't know.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:36.934
I think I'm just going to pick
up the bike first, you know?

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.567
[ Laughter ]
I don't want to be

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.701
the only guy out there
without a bike, you know?

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:43.667
[ Laughter ]
And then I'll just take it
down there with me.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:47.167
And once you get it down there,
you got to bring it back up.

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.567
[ Laughter ]
And then maybe I can get an Uber

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.868
and put it in the back of the
Uber, something like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.133
I just want to get somewhere

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.767
where I can ride this thing,
you know?

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.934
[ Laughter ]
Been paying for it all day long.

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:03.734
This is a tough city
to get around.

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.000
You ever give someone directions
in New York City

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.400
and then, two blocks later,
just go...

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:14.434
..."Oh, no.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:16.267
I think I killed
that foreign family.

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:17.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.934
They are so dead
and there's nothing I can do."

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:22.133
[ Laughter ]
I just want to call 911

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.634
and be like, "I'm so sorry.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.467
There's this family

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:27.634
and I sent them west
at Port Authority

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
and all they wanted
was cheesecake

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:32.701
and now, I can't sleep."

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:36.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.701
My family's concerned
about me out here

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:40.300
and they should be.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.167
[ Laughter ]
If you're a criminal

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.501
and you see me walking around,

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.701
your thought is,
"It's going to be a good day."

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:48.501
[ Laughter ]
That's what you think.

00:04:48.501 --> 00:04:51.200
"I'm going to hit my quota early
and clock out, you know?"

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.534
Criminal half day.

00:04:55.534 --> 00:04:57.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.434
Like if I was ever on the phone

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:00.767
with my father,
walking around the city,

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.467
he'd always go,
"Son, where's your wallet?

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.167
Put your wallet
in your front pocket."

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:09.367
That was my dad's plan to foil
New York City's criminals.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.734
Just to switch my wallet

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:14.167
over into the unexpected pocket
you know?

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:16.634
[ Laughter ]
I don't know how this plays out,

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:17.901
if you get held up, you know?

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:19.601
it's like, "I hope
they don't come around.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:21.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:21.734 --> 00:05:23.868
I can't believe I'm getting
away with it right now.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:26.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.901
My father's going
to be so proud."

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:29.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:29.701 --> 00:05:31.300
"Where's the wallet, man?!
Where's the --"

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.400
[ Snickers ]

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.400
I mean --

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.100
[ Cheering ]

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:44.100
This guy has no clue!

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.300
What a rube, huh?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:48.567
I guess he's never been
to Idaho before.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:49.868
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.467
I'm Ryan Hamilton.

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:52.501
Thank you very much.

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:53.667
[ Whistling ]

00:05:55.534 --> 00:05:57.100
-Oh, my gosh!

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.367
Thank you so much.

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:00.300
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.634
Ryan Hamilton!

00:06:01.634 --> 00:06:04.367
That's how you do it
right there.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:08.000
For more info,
go to ryanhamiltonlive.com.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.167
We'll be right back.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:11.133
Oh, my gosh!

